@startuml
title VirtualMotionTracker System Architecture
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

' External system
component "User Application" as UserApp <<External>>

' Runtime dependency
component "SteamVR / OpenVR Runtime" as Steam <<Runtime>>

package "VirtualMotionTracker" {
  component "VMT Manager" as Manager
  component "VMT Driver" as Driver <<OpenVR Driver>>

  node "Shared Memory (IPC)" as IPC {
    component "Manager -> Driver\nJSON Channel" as M2D <<JSON>>
    component "Driver -> Manager\nJSON Channel" as D2M <<JSON>>
  }

  artifact "Legacy Binding\nJSON (controller_type: mycontroller)" as Binding <<JSON>>
}

' External control input (OSC) to Manager
UserApp ..> Manager : OSC control input
note on link
No fixed port or complete command set specified
end note

' Shared-memory JSON channels with synchronization metadata
Manager --> M2D : write JSON
M2D --> Driver : read JSON

Driver --> D2M : write JSON
D2M --> Manager : read JSON

note right of M2D
Shared-memory control fields:
- send_count
- handshake_count
- message_length
end note

note right of D2M
Shared-memory control fields:
- send_count
- handshake_count
- message_length
end note

' Driver integration with SteamVR/OpenVR runtime
Driver --> Steam : OpenVR driver interface

' Legacy controller binding artifact flow
Driver ..> Binding : provides / installs
Binding ..> Steam : consumed by runtime

note right of Binding
Legacy mapping (right-hand):
- /user/hand/right/input/a -> /actions/legacy/in/right_axis1_press
- /user/hand/right/input/c -> /actions/legacy/in/right_a_press
- /user/hand/right/input/b -> /actions/legacy/in/right_grip_press
Mode: button, parameters.sub_mode: complex
end note

' Dependency context note
note right of Driver
OpenVR SDK behaviors (init, interface-version checks, shutdown,
path constants, SDK structures) are dependency context, not core
product functionality.
end note

@enduml
